From 33c59161098ee7712323ba35178743e1cc4a07f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:49:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AUTO_MEMORIES_REGFILES: a register file in place of an
 inferred memory, through a seam yosys makes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Many cores keep the register file inline, an array in the CPU module
with no module boundary a spec could name: Rocket's rf, picorv32's
cpuregs. A spec's `memory <module>.<cell>` key now names the memory
yosys infers there, and the register file takes its place:
gen_memories.py writes a memlib entry and a techmap wrapper from the
spec, and synthesis, while it reads the sources, maps that one memory to
an instance of the register file (memory_libmap, techmap) before
hierarchy would prune the file's module, then reads the generated
netlist as its body. The memory is found by its cell and its module's
definition and selected by attribute, so no slang $ name is spelled;
opt -full, scoped to the modules holding one, makes Chisel's per-bit
write enables one signal, without which memory_libmap splits the array
into one-bit slices. A memory not found once, or not mapped to one
instance, stops the build. Such a file is always inlined.

asap7/tinyRocket-regfile is Rocket's integer register file this way
(RocketCore's _T_288, 31 x 32, 2R1W), the RTL unchanged; tinyRocket's
config takes a nickname from the including design. To global route:
3777 um2 against tinyRocket's 3956, 32 clock gates.

Not upstreamed. Retires at a //:bump onto an ORFS that carries it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
