diff --git a/docs/user/AutoMemories.md b/docs/user/AutoMemories.md
index c4f5e03ce..2b1387718 100644
--- a/docs/user/AutoMemories.md
+++ b/docs/user/AutoMemories.md
@@ -167,6 +167,36 @@ on `AUTO_MEMORIES_MACRO_PLACE`, the register files to place as macros:
   the end. A large design whose floorplan plans its register files lists
   them.
 
+### A register file with no module of its own
+
+Many cores keep the register file inline: an array in the CPU module
+(Rocket's `rf`, picorv32's `cpuregs`), with no module boundary a spec
+could name. A spec's `memory <module>.<cell>` key names the memory yosys
+infers there instead, and the register file takes its place through a
+seam synthesis makes:
+
+```
+module rocket_rf
+memory Rocket._T_288
+words 32
+bits 32
+clock clk
+read raddr0 rdata0
+read raddr1 rdata1
+write waddr wdata wen
+...
+```
+
+The module and its ports are the spec's own. `gen_memories.py` writes a
+memlib entry (`<m>.memlib`: one clocked write port per `write`, sharing
+the clock, one combinational read port per `read`) and a techmap wrapper
+(`<m>_map.v`) that instantiates the register file; synthesis, while it
+reads the sources, runs `memory_libmap` on that one memory and `techmap`,
+then reads the generated netlist as the register file's body. Such a file
+is always inlined. A memory that is not found once, or that does not map
+to one instance, stops the build. `designs/asap7/tinyRocket-regfile` is
+Rocket's integer register file this way, the RTL unchanged.
+
 A word holds its value between writes either through a hold term in
 every bit's write mux (`write_style mux`, the default) or through one
 integrated clock gate per word, enabled by its write selects
